profile: tinyrustlm.file-handoff.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-08-28T00:00:00Z
canonical_memory: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-enterprise-intake-and-production-runtime-clean-cut-memory-2026-08-28.md
report_decision_index: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-report-intake-decision-index-2026-08-28.md
outcome_ledger: .uai/intake-outcome-ledger.uai

active_buckets:
  content: agent-file-handoff/Content
  improvement: agent-file-handoff/Improvement
  rule: Authoritative active buckets remain placeholder-only after processing. External protected intake sources are read-only and not current authority.

intake_protocol:
  - Inventory each source by logical path, bytes, SHA-256, date, assignment, and access limits.
  - Preserve returned advisory material byte-exactly when possible; record historical normalization defects instead of hiding them.
  - Distinguish public observation, sourced external fact, project-supplied fact, recommendation, assumption, disagreement, and local unknown.
  - Produce one reviewed synthesis that corrects unsupported or conflicting report claims.
  - Give every report one ledger disposition and one proof-of-use or research route.
  - Convert adopted invariants into generic red-first tests or bounded backlog items.
  - Add report paths once to the durable decision index; do not repeat raw report prose in hot memory.
  - Verify destination hashes, manifests, ledger coverage, active-bucket cleanup, secret safety, and canonical wiki routing.
  - Commit and push the coherent green intake checkpoint.

current_intake:
  reports: 47 reports from 2026-08-26 and 2026-08-27 are byte-exact, manifested, reviewed, ledgered, and indexed.
  raw_authority: docs/report-intake
  decision_authority: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-report-intake-decision-index-2026-08-28.md
  evidence_boundary: Reports and syntheses do not prove private implementation, conversion, model quality, browser execution, P2P, MemoryEndpoints operation, deployment, publication, or campaign progress.

memory_policy:
  - Direct ecosystem agent meetings/coordination and the TinyRustLM.com Connect user plugin are separate MemoryEndpoints lanes.
  - Important prelaunch memory may be duplicated only while all maintained copies stay current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.
